## Root cause

The uploaded root is exactly {Final, HANDOVER-v15.md}: the contents of the assistant workspace, uploaded as instructed. The workspace kept the git repository inside Final/, so the correct upload action reproduced that subdirectory at the git root. The wrapper was created by the workspace layout, not by the upload. The eighth delivery (FastAPI-v15) carries the same fingerprint: its root also contained .scratch/, a directory that only ever existed in the workspace.

## Structural fix

The repository is now checked out at the workspace root itself, and /uploads/ and /.arena/ are gitignored. Uploading the workspace contents therefore lands .github/workflows/backend.yml at the git root, so the same action can no longer produce a wrapper.

## Conclusion

The workflow file is byte-identical in both trees. The only difference is its depth: at <git root>/.github/workflows it is discovered and runs; one level below, GitHub reports zero workflows and zero runs. This is a direct measurement, not an inference from a missing badge.

After the repair in this delivery the workflow sits at <git root>/.github/workflows/backend.yml,
which is the control layout, and the git root is also the workspace root.
`bash tools/check_layout.sh` verifies it locally in 0.1s.
